<title>GERMANY: German grain trade seeks to export free mkt grain.</title>
<headline>German grain trade seeks to export free mkt grain.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>German grain traders placed bids to export 206,200 tonnes of soft wheat, with rebates in a 16.73 to 18.93 Ecus a tonne range, grain traders said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Traders also applied for rebates in a 27.95-30.70 Ecus per tonne range for the export of 91,550 tonnes of free market barley and bid for a 31.99 Ecus subsidy for the export of 2,000 tonnes of free market rye.</p>
<p>--Hamburg newsroom +49-40-41903275</p>
